---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Cards from '../../components/Cards.astro';
import {categories,archive} from '../../lib/content';
export function getStaticPaths(){return categories.map(category=>({params:{slug:category.slug},props:{category}}))}
const {category}=Astro.props;
const entries=archive.filter(a=>a.categories.includes(category.name));
const picks=entries.slice(0,3);
const intros:Record<string,string>={
'simple-living':'Simple living is less about owning a particular number of things than about making everyday choices with a little more intention. There is no required aesthetic, rigid routine or finish line. Start with what regularly drains your time, money or attention, then look for one change that would genuinely help.',
'decluttering':'A useful home does not have to look empty. Decluttering is the practical work of deciding what supports your life now, what needs a better place and what can leave responsibly. These guides offer manageable starting points without asking you to clear a whole house in a weekend.',
'organization':'The best organizing system is one you can use on an ordinary, busy day. A basket by the door, a place for incoming mail or a shorter evening reset can help more than a room full of matching containers. Begin with the point where your routine gets stuck.',
'house-home':'A home earns its comfort through the everyday things that happen inside it: cooking, resting, sharing meals and finding what you need. Explore practical approaches to cleaning, laundry, kitchen routines and the small changes that make a space easier to live in, without chasing a showroom standard.',
'frugality':'Spending less is useful when it protects something that matters to you, whether that is breathing room in a budget, a future plan or fewer financial surprises. These articles look at the trade-offs behind everyday purchases, affordable enjoyment and choosing enough without turning every decision into a deprivation contest.',
'relationships':'Good relationships need more than a tidy calendar or the perfect phrase. They benefit from honest attention, clear boundaries and small actions that can be repeated. Explore thoughtful ways to communicate care, make room for other people and notice when a relationship asks for a different kind of response.',
'happiness':'Enjoyment rarely follows a perfect schedule. It can come from a little rest, a modest pleasure, a conversation or permission to do something without being good at it. These guides explore everyday satisfaction without promising constant positivity or treating difficult feelings as a failure to think correctly.',
'productivity':'Being productive does not mean filling every spare minute. It means making useful progress while leaving enough attention for the rest of your life. These guides consider work habits, realistic priorities, boundaries and simpler systems that reduce repeated decisions rather than add another demanding routine to your day.',
'personal-development':'Personal growth can be quiet, practical and unfinished. It might mean trying a new activity, asking a more useful question or noticing a standard that no longer serves you. These articles make space for experimentation and changing your mind, rather than presenting one ideal version of a successful life.',
'health':'A calmer daily life can support well-being, but no lifestyle routine solves every health concern. These articles discuss accessible habits, rest, mental space and growing older with care. They offer general information rather than diagnosis or treatment, and encourage professional support whenever a concern needs individual attention.'};
---
<Base title={category.name} description={`Practical ${category.name.toLowerCase()} guides from On Simplicity: thoughtful ideas for a calmer, more manageable everyday life.`} breadcrumbs={[{name:'Home',path:'/'},{name:category.name}]}><header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">The journal / {category.name}</p><h1>{category.name}</h1></header><div class="category-intro prose prose-stone max-w-none"><p>{intros[category.slug]}</p><p>For a useful starting point, explore {picks.map((a,i)=><Fragment>{i>0?(i===picks.length-1?' or ':', '):''}<a href={a.path}>{a.title}</a></Fragment>)}. Choose the idea that fits your circumstances and adapt it rather than taking on everything at once. If the next step involves finding practical help rather than another do-it-yourself task, our <a href="/resource-partners/">Resource Partners directory</a> offers business profiles and articles to help you research your options. A useful change should make your day easier, not give you another standard to meet.</p></div><section class="section"><h2 class="sr-only">All {category.name} articles</h2><Cards entries={entries}/></section></Base>
